# Who reviews what.
#
# GitHub reads this file from top to bottom and the LAST matching pattern wins, so the default
# rule comes first and the security-sensitive paths are listed after it.
#
# `@scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers` must be a team (or set of users) with write access to this
# repository. If the organisation names its team differently, update every line below.

# Default owner for everything in the repository.
*                                   @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers

# Deployed, value-bearing Soroban contracts. A merged change here can alter token, NFT or
# governance behaviour for every deployed instance, so these paths require an owner review.
/contracts/                         @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers

# CI. The workflow controls what runs on every pull request and holds the repository token.
/.github/                           @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers
/.github/workflows/                 @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers

# Root manifests and the toolchain pin decide what is built and with which compiler.
/Cargo.toml                         @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers
/Cargo.lock                         @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers
/rust-toolchain.toml                @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers
/package.json                       @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers
/package-lock.json                  @scaffold-studio-hq/maintainers
